assert_eq(load64(_r3_br), GEO_CAP_START_CAP, "... on the start cap");
# Its copy solves the barrel on the scaled path, as round 2 did at the tiny size: positions
# (5, 8, 0), (0,0,0)-(0,0,-16), r = 10, all times 2^-1074, along (6, 8, 0) 2^-1074: the exit
# 0.0568, 0.78 ulp (its classic quadratic at the copy's size: 10.2 ulp).
# [measured: C336 fixture probe (fx3) and exact Fraction/Decimal values, 3.3.5 and round 2 vs this tree, 2026-10-11]
