# === 3.4.1 GEO6: GEO4's unkilled mutants ===
test_group("3.4.1 GEO6: GEO4's unkilled mutants");
# The review's rows for B3, E3, C1, F3 and F6, each pinned. F6 dies on its row, E3 on a row of its own below. B3,
# C1 and F3 do not die: M4's repair took away what each could reach. B3: with a true e a hit's root test implies
# dl > ed and both ed's read a miss alike. C1: a near root on the segment is where the line enters the cylinder,
# so no cap comes first. F3: the certificate's piece is 4 eta from any plane, where the copy's label agrees. F4 is
# equivalent: a copy miss has cb = GEO_FACE_NONE, never the certificate's piece, so the other half of that test
# routes it; tc = 0 with a piece needs a contact at the copy's origin, at least 8 (|ab| + r) from the capsule.
# [measured: GEO6 3.4.1 kl.py and ct.py over the families, 54,000 far rows, s22 / mutants / this tree, 2026-11-01]
